  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Two roots of the cubic equation $x^3+ax^2+bx+24=0$ are $4$ and $-2$. Find the values of $a$ and $b$ and hence state the equation of the cubic.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=-5$, $b=-2$; $x^3-5x^2-2x+24=0$.",
      "worked": "Let the third root be $\\gamma$. Using the product of roots,\n$$\\begin{aligned}(4)(-2)\\gamma&=-24\\\\\\gamma&=3.\\end{aligned}$$\nUsing the sum of roots,\n$$\\begin{aligned}4-2+3&=-a\\\\a&=-5.\\end{aligned}$$\nUsing the sum of products taken two at a time,\n$$\\begin{aligned}b&=(4)(-2)+(4)(3)+(-2)(3)\\\\&=-8+12-6\\\\&=-2.\\end{aligned}$$\nHence the cubic equation is $x^3-5x^2-2x+24=0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 33
  },
